{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446635-true-fae-titles","id":1446635,"title":"True Fae Titles","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-30T10:54:19-07:00","id":1446635,"title":"True Fae Titles","content":"Instead of blessings or dread powers, a <i>True Fae\u2019s </i>base abilities should be their titles. Their titles are the sources of their powers and existence. Like contracts, I think their should be common, royal, and even imperial titles.<br /> <br /> As examples, here are the titles of a <i>True Fae </i>who is a manifestation of the concepts of the fairytale <b><i>Beauty and the Beast </i></b>and the fairytale concept, <i>Prince Charming. </i>He is also the Oberon from Shakespeare\u2019s <i>Midsummer Night\u2019s Dream</i> and Titania\u2019s former keeper.<br /> <br /> In Beast form, his titles are <b><i>Monster</i></b> and <b><i>Lord of Beasts.</i></b><br /> <br /> As <i>Prince Charming, </i>His titles are <b><i>Fairest of Them All </i></b>and <b><i>Knight in Shining Armor.</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>Note: I designed these titles that unless you are a wyrd 10 changeling with high attributes and skills, the Gentry is going to stomp on you like a sumo belly dancer.</i><br /> <br /> <b><i>Monster</i></b><br /> The <i>Monster</i> has a bite attack that does +3 aggravated damage without needing to grapple.<br /> <br /> They have claws that do +2 aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> The <i>Monster</i> never suffers perception penalties due to darkness, smoke, or mist and they can track a target by sniffing their emotions.<br /> Any mortal that sees the <i>Monster</i> suffers the frightened condition and can not use their will power against the <i>Monster</i>. The find themselves moving to obey the <i>Monster\u2019s </i>commands, though changelings can make a resolve + composure + wyrd roll against the <i>Monster.</i><br /> <br /> By Spending a point of glamor, the gentry can blend in with their surrounding and make a jump scare against an opponent, giving them the frightened condition. They can also choose to make a surprise attack against an opponent and do not suffer penalties when making such an attack.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Lord of Beasts</i></b><br /> <br /> The Gentry can communicate with ordinary animals as a standard action with most animals treating the gentry as a trusted ally.<br /> <br /> The Gentry can harvest glamor from animals.<br /> <br /> Most animals will obey the Gentry\u2019s command as long as it does not lead to their destruction.<br /> <br /> By spending a point a glamor, the Gentry can make a bestial cry and summon a group/pack of animals that will track a specific target for the Gentry.<br /> <br /> The Gentry can send animals into a murderous frenzy against a specific individual by make a successful presence+ animal kenneling+ wyrd against a target<br /> By roaring, the Gentry can cause all mortal listeners who hear the call to fall into the lunacy condition, though changelings are immune to this affect<br /> <br /> <b><i>Frailty</i></b> This title will not work on any animal who has a bond of loyalty to a specific human or changeling<br /> <br /> <b>Knight in Shining Armor</b><br /> <br /> <i>The Knight</i> is immune to surprise attacks and instantly recognizes a character\u2019s fighting style<br /> <br /> <i>The Knight</i> never suffers defense penalties due to armor, initiative penalties due to weaponry or multiple opponent penalties.<br /> <br /> <i>The Knight </i>always draws his blade as a reflexive action.<br /> <br /> <i>The Knight</i> counts all weaponry successes three times instead of once.<br /> <br /> <i>The Knight </i>can parry a ranged attack back at an opponent<br /> <br /> <i>The Knight </i>can attack all opponents within 32 yards at his full weaponry dice pool.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Frailty </i></b>The Knight must always follow the code of chivalry or he greatly reduces his power.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Fairest of Them All</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>The Gentry</i> gains four automatic successes in all roll where appearance can help.<br /> <br /> <i>The True Fae\u2019s</i> beauty is such that mortal men find themselves automatically moving to follow his commands and mortal women feel a passionate love upon gazing upon him and gain the <i>Fae Struck</i> condition. Changelings can resist this power by making a resolve +composure+ wyrd roll.<br /> <br /> Mortals can not bring themselves to attack him, unless he attacks them first. Anyone who attacks him suffers a -2 dice penalty to their attack pool.<br /> <br /> By speaking to a or group of mortals, by making a Presence + Persuasion + wyrd roll against them and his successful, the mortals worship him as a god.<br /> <br /> By gently caressing an individual, the gentry can cause the <b><i>Ravished </i></b>condition which becomes the <b>Bacchanalia </b>tilt.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Frailty: </i></b>Gentry with this title are supposed to represent the ideals of romantic love. However, they are much too selfish to feel this emotion. As a result, this title will not work on any character motivated by true love or true friendship.<br /> <br /> <i>Loophole: </i>This title can still work if a character has come to take their romantic relationships or friendships for granted. Though their feelings will eventually allow them to break the control the <i>Gentry </i>has on them.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Fae-Struck Condition: </i></b>The characters feel an all-consuming love for the fairest that overrides self-preservation. They will walk thousands of miles, commit murder, or acts of terrorism just to be near the <i>Gentry</i>.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Ravished Condition: </i></b>The character feels waves of ecstasy so great that they are knocked unconscious. <br /> <br /> <b>Bacchanalia <i>Tilt: </i></b>The ecstasy the character feels are so strong it damages their body. The character suffers seven points of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T07:43:41-07:00","id":1446977,"title":"","content":"Some legends claim that fairies are demons or fallen angels. These Titles belong to a <i>True Fae </i>who is a manifestation of that idea.<br /> <br /> He has two miens;<br /> When he is <b><i>The Dark Man</i></b>, he aims to corrupt a community/town, his Titles are <i>Lord of Darkness </i>and<i> Devil</i>.<br /> <br /> When he is <b><i>The Beast</i></b> and means to wreck havoc, his Titles are <i>Monster</i> and <i>Demon.</i><br /> <br /> <b><i>Lord of Darkness</i></b><br /> <br /> The <i>Gentry </i>never suffers penalties due to darkness, including supernatural darkness.<br /> <br /> <i>The Gentry </i>can use shadows to observe what is happening in the mortal realm.<br /> <br /> <i>The Gentry </i>is as fluid as shadow. They always have a full defense dice pool and never suffer penalties due to ranged and coordinated attacks. They can move at full speed under door frames, though cracks, and the creases between floor boards.<br /> <br /> By spending a point of glamor, <i>The True Fae </i>can use shadows to teleport anywhere in the mortal realm.<br /> <br /> <i>The Gentry</i> can spend a point of glamor to craft artifacts out of shadows.<br /> <br /> <i>The Gentry </i>can spend a point of glamor and animate the nearby shadows to sentience to serve him.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Frailty: </i></b><i>The Gentry </i>suffers aggravated damage from sunlight and fire, and non-soakable bashing damage from intense bright light.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Devil</i></b><br /> People have sense of familiarity with <i>The Devil, </i>though they are not sure from where.<br /> <br /> Criminals and creatures of darkness like vampires and styx have difficulty raising a hand against <i>The Devil, </i>and <i>The Devil </i>never suffers penalties when getting them to perform some service for him.<br /> <br /> <i>The Devil\u2019s </i>always appears as something his audience finds comforting and sympathetic. <i>They Devil</i> always has persuasion and subterfuge pools of 6 or higher and characters suffer -2 to accurately describe him.<br /> <br /> People feel comfortable sharing their darkest secrets and desires with him, though changelings can make a resolve + composure +wyrd to resist this effect.<br /> <i>The Devil </i>can look at the person and automatically gains the informed condition about them; their virtue, vice, highest and lowest attributes and skills, what they have in their pocket, their mistakes, and insecurities.<br /> <br /> By spending a dot a glamor and making a successful Manipulate + Subterfuge roll against a character\u2019s Composure +Wyrd, <i>The Devil </i>can make a characters act out one of their darkest and most debased desires.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Frailties: </i></b><i>The Devil </i>suffers aggravated damage from stepping on hollowed ground or touching holy objects. <i>The Devil </i>suffers non-soakable bashing damage from hearing prayers spoken by one of the truly faithful. <i>The Devil\u2019s </i>powers will not work on the truly faithful, the truly innocent, and people who have a fascination with practical jokes and parlor tricks.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Demon</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>The Demon </i>never suffers penalties due to burning or cold effects.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Wings of the Damned: </i></b><i>The Demon </i>has wings that allow him to fly at 300 mph while carrying 1,000 pounds. These wings can also be used as weapons by creating gusts of wind that blow <i>The Demon\u2019s </i>opponents off their feet.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Hellish Fury: </i></b><i>The Demon </i>can make three attacks per turn.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Hellish Might: </i></b><i>The Demon raises their strength and stamina to 12 instead being limited to six.</i><br /> <br /> <b><i>Dragon Scales: </i></b><i>The Demon </i>has scales that are immune to bashing damage and can soak aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Burning Furnace: </i></b>By making a successful Dexterity + Brawl attack against an opponent, <i>The Demon </i>breaths fire that deals aggravated damage. <i>The Demon </i>is also hot to the touch and anyone that tries to touch them suffers +2 lethal burning damage.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Face of Evil: </i></b><i>The Demon\u2019s </i>mien is so unclean that mortals that gaze upon it suffer the lunacy condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Frailties: </b><i>The Demon </i>suffers aggravated damage from stepping on hollowed ground or touching holy objects. <i>The Demon </i>suffers non-soakable bashing damage from hearing prayers spoken by one of the truly faithful. <i>The Demon\u2019s </i>powers will not work on the truly faithful, the truly innocent.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-02T17:27:34-07:00","id":1447060,"title":"","content":"Here are some more thoughts on <i>True Fae </i>Titles. I was disappointed when the 2e Corebook emphasized that it was causal indifference into whether or not the <i>True Fae</i> tried to get back their changeling or targeted specific humans. So I wanted to emphasize how<i> True Fae</i> are bound to humanity through their Titles.<br /> <br /> 1. The Titles of the <i>True Fae </i>are born from the fables, fairytales, folklore, and mythology of humanity. As such, True Fae are living manifestations of our stories.<br /> <br /> 2. <i>True Fae</i> can edit/refine their <i>Titles </i>through the actions of their changelings in their realms in Arcadia.<br /> <br /> 3. How popular and well known the stories a <i>True Fae's </i> Titles are connected are, greatly influences their power and the <i>True Fae's </i>connection to the mortal realm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T21:08:40-07:00","id":1447332,"title":"","content":"Here is one of the common titles of <i>The True Fae/Gentry.</i> Meaning the title is wide spread among the <i>Gentry.</i><br /> <br /> <b><i>Witch </i></b><br /> <br /> <i>The Witch </i>can see major events in a character\u2019s past and present, as well as the potential roads of the future.<br /> <br /> <i>The Witch</i> can smell lies with each lie having a distinct scent. <i>Note: No Dice roll or glamor is needed for this power.</i><br /> <br /> In environments where there is a fierce wind or storm tilt, the witch can fly through the air like a ghost.<br /> <br /> By spending a point of glamor,<i> The Witch </i>can turn an animal into its familiar. <i>The Witch</i> can use their familiar\u2019s senses, channel their contracts and other powers through. <i>The Witch </i>can make up to six animals, at once, her familiar.<br /> <br /> By spending a point of glamor, <i>The Witch </i>can use any reflective surface for scrying.<br /> <br /> By spending a point of glamor, <i>The Witch</i> can cause one of the following curses. <i>Note: The Witch rolls Presence + Occult +Wyrd against a targets Resolve + Composure + Wyrd.</i><ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b><i>Hag\u2019s Visage</i></b>: The target becomes monstrously ugly causing people to suffer the frightened or insenate tilts.</li> <li><b><i>Goblin\u2019s Kiss: </i></b>The target turns to stone.</li> <li><b><i>Goblin Luck:</i></b> For each success, the target loses a dot in either contacts, resources, even a contract or pledge.</li> <li><b><i>Devil\u2019s Dance:</i></b> By singing or playing a musical instrument, <i>The Witch </i>can cause an audience to dance to death.</li> <li><b><i>Plague:</i></b> <i>The Witch </i>curses a target with a supernatural illness that causes the target to rise up as an undead after death. This illness can be cured by supernatural means like a contract, certain goblin fruit, or spell.</li> </ol><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T22:03:45-07:00","id":1447344,"title":"","content":"Almost none of these fit the definition of Titles laid out in both editions of the game \u2014 you're basically just listing archetypes akin to those described in Autumn Nightmares.<br /> <br /> The Fae aren't manifestations of stories or ideas \u2014 at least in First Edition, they're bits of the fabric of destiny that've tangled their way into precarious individuality and godlike ability, whose relation to archetypal figures of human myth is secondary to the fact that they're a face for divine power expressed in parseable fashion and therefore tend to be working with memorable forces in ways people can identify. They're narratives because they order the world around them at an essential level, not because the works of Andersen, Perrault, Grimm, Carroll, et al hold some especial significance to their general templates.<br /> <br /> Second Edition may change some of the particulars of how these work, but the Fae still have more to their existence than acting out fairytale roles for the sake of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T22:18:46-07:00","id":1447347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446635-true-fae-titles?p=1447344#post1447344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost none of these fit the definition of Titles laid out in both editions of the game \u2014 you're basically just listing archetypes akin to those described in Autumn Nightmares.<br /> <br /> The Fae aren't manifestations of stories or ideas \u2014 at least in First Edition, they're bits of the fabric of destiny that've tangled their way into precarious individuality and godlike ability, whose relation to archetypal figures of human myth is secondary to the fact that they're a face for divine power expressed in parseable fashion and therefore tend to be working with memorable forces in ways people can identify. They're narratives because they order the world around them at an essential level, not because the works of Andersen, Perrault, Grimm, Carroll, et al hold some especial significance to their general templates.<br /> <br /> Second Edition may change some of the particulars of how these work, but the Fae still have more to their existence than acting out fairytale roles for the sake of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> We've have seen a lot of changes between 1st and 2nd edition. I would also point out that many of the tales of Anderson, Perrault, and Grimm Long before they put them to pen and paper and there are MANY different variation of the tales in their actions.<br /> <br /> The way I envision it, what the fabric of destiny got tangled in was the beliefs and fears of man born from the fables and stories they told. This gave the stories a sense of awareness and even form, which is malleable based on the stories, dreams, and fears that the true fae come to feed on, AND how the stories change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T22:25:28-07:00","id":1447348,"title":"","content":"The closes example I could think of are the <i>Deadlights </i> from Stephen King's <i><b>It,</b></i> was a amorphous light until the human mind gave it the form of a spider, and then it took the form of <i>Pennywise</i> and many other identities based on the dreams, nightmares of the children of <i>Dairy</i>, though that isn't an accurate comparison...<br /> <br /> Essentially, the first glamor, which gave <i>The True Fae</i> existence and awareness were the fears and desires represented by the first stories and superstitions humanity created to explain certain disasters and world phenomenon. <i>The True Fae</i> were able to claim/ draw on more stories/titles to give their identity/ mien a more unique form/personality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-03T22:26:47-07:00","id":1447349,"title":"","content":"Titles are not the SOULS of the <i>True Fae</i>, but they are the mind and body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-04T17:50:39-07:00","id":1447499,"title":"","content":"Many fairy creatures are said to be a type of ghost and their many Celtic gods of death who later become sidhe/fae.<br /> <br /> <i>The True Fae</i> who hold the title, <i><b>Lord of the Dead</b></i>, are a manifestation of that belief.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Lord of the Dead</i></b><br /> <br /> The Gentry can navigate the shadowlands and underworld as easily as if it were the hedge.<br /> <br /> The <i>True Fae</i> can see, hear, communicate with, and even touch ghosts and spirits. They can also tell if a person, object, or place is a fetter.<br /> <br /> The <i>True Fae</i> can see death marks on people and places. They can also detect a death that is happening up to six street blocks away. <i>Note: No dice roll or glamor is needed for any of these powers.</i><br /> <br /> The <i>True Fae</i> can take control of any supernatural power associated with death like a werewolf\u2019s <b><i>Gifts of death</i></b> or a mage\u2019s <b><i>Arcana of Death.</i></b><br /> <br /> By spending a dot of glamor, the True Fae can animate nearby corpses into zombies that serve them.<br /> <br /> By spending a dot of glamor, the True Fae can curse/kill a mortal and control how they die; such as dying in a car crash, getting electrocuted in a bath tub, being murdered in their home ect.<br /> <i>Note: The Final Destination series was a HUGE source of inspiration for the last power.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-05-19T18:46:46-07:00","id":1449072,"title":"","content":"Here is another idea for a <i>True Fae</i> title.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Giant</i></b><br /> <br /> The Giant has a size of 40.<br /> <br /> The Giant has a strength of 16 and a stamina 15.<br /> <br /> The Giant causes the earthquake tilt by walking.<br /> <br /> The Giant can swallow an object up to size 20 whole.<br /> <br /> When the Giant makes a successful attack +9 points of lethal damage.<br /> <br /> When the Giant throws an object add 3 miles to the distance it lands.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Frailty: Like Goliath, the giants weakness is its head. If you manage to strike the forehead with a rock thrown from a slingshot, the giant suffers aggravated damage and is potentially banished from the mortal realm for a period of time.</i></b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T20:06:50-07:00","id":1450905,"title":"","content":"I have made some edits to some of the True Fae titles I made. I would like to hear if anyone has any suggestions or thoughts.<br /> <br /> Some Fairy mythos claims that fairies are fallen angels, or demons. I wanted to create titles that allow the story teller to play with this idea. I also want to give them the avenue to explore how many aspects of pagan lore was taken and incorporated into the Christian understanding of hell, demons, and the devil. For example, Pan\u2019s goat horns and legs became the devil\u2019s horns and cloven hooves, while Poseidon\u2019s trident became the devil\u2019s pitch fork. With the following titles, I hope to give the story teller ideas on how to use the different themes associated with demons.<br /> Demons are often portrayed as spirits of darkness that can manipulate natural darkness and the darkness in the hearts of man. Below is a True Fae title that portrays this idea.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Lord of Darkness</i></b><br /> <br /> The <i>Lord of Darkness </i>never suffers penalties due to darkness, including supernatural darkness.<br /> <br /> <i>The Lord of Darkness </i>can use shadows to observe what is happening in the mortal realm.<br /> <br /> <i>The Lord of Darkness </i>can look at a mortal and see the darkness within them. They know what a character\u2019s vice is, what flaws they possess, as well as their darkest secrets and desires. <i>The</i> <i>Lord of Darkness</i> can use this information to give the character the frightened or insensate tilt.<br /> <br /> <i>The Lord of Darkness </i>can control evil beings. Criminals, Pure tribe werewolves, styx, and vampires can not bring themselves to harm the Gentry, provide him with information/gossip, and even obey orders he gives them.<br /> <br /> <i>The Lord of Darkness </i>is as fluid as shadow. They always have a full defense dice pool and never suffer penalties due to ranged and coordinated attacks. They can move at full speed under door frames, though cracks, and the creases between floor boards.<br /> <br /> By spending a point of glamor, <i>The True Fae </i>can use shadows to teleport up to 100 miles away in the mortal realm.<br /> <br /> <i>The Gentry</i> can spend a point of glamor to craft artifacts out of shadows.<br /> <br /> <i>The Gentry </i>can spend a point of glamor and animate the nearby shadows to sentience to serve him.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Frailty: </i></b><i>The Gentry </i>suffers aggravated damage from sunlight and fire, and non-soakable bashing damage from intense bright light.<br /> <br /> The Devil is portrayed as a master salesman of the soul, a corrupter and conman extraordinaire. This True Fae title is a manifestation of that idea, though I do admit is was inspired by Leland Gaunt from <b><i>Needful Things.</i></b><br /> <br /> <b><i>Devil</i></b><br /> <br /> People have sense of familiarity with <i>The Devil, </i>though they are not sure from where.<br /> <br /> <i>The Devil\u2019s </i>always appears as something his audience finds comforting and sympathetic. The <i>Devil</i> also always says the right thing at the right time and even finish people\u2019s sentences. <i>They Devil</i> always has persuasion and subterfuge pools of 6 or higher and characters suffer -2 to accurately describe him.<br /> <br /> <i>The Devil </i>can look at the person and automatically gains the informed condition about them; their virtue, vice, highest and lowest attributes and skills, what they have in their pocket, their mistakes, and insecurities.<br /> <br /> <i>The Devil </i>gains three automatic successes in understanding how a market works in region, whether in the Hedge or mortal realm. This includes the social dynamics, popular products, how the export import system in the region works.<br /> <br /> By spending a dot a glamor and making a successful manipulate + subterfuge roll against a character\u2019s composure + wyrd, <i>The Devil </i>can make a characters act out one of their darkest and most debased desires.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Frailties: </i></b><i>The Devil </i>suffers aggravated damage from stepping on hollowed ground or touching holy objects. <i>The Devil </i>suffers non-soakable bashing damage from hearing prayers spoken by one of the truly faithful. <i>The Devil\u2019s </i>powers will not work on the truly faithful, the truly innocent, and people who have a fascination with practical jokes and parlor tricks.<br /> <br /> I can see a lot of story tellers having fun by just portraying the demonic Gentry as a being of infernal destruction. The below title is meant to be used when the Gentry will visit raw destruction on the mortal realm.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Demon</i></b><br /> <br /> <i>The Demon </i>never suffers penalties due to burning or cold effects.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Wings of the Damned: </i></b><i>The Demon </i>has wings that allow him to fly at 300 mph while carrying 1,000 pounds. These wings can also be used as weapons by creating gusts of wind that blow <i>The Demon\u2019s </i>opponents off their feet.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Hellish Fury: </i></b><i>The Demon </i>can make three attacks per turn.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Pestilence: </i></b>The very presence of the demon summons swarms of vermin. The Demon presence is heralded with locusts, cockroaches, rats, and bats swarming the community.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Hellish Might: </i></b><i>The Demon raises their strength and stamina to 12 instead being limited to six.</i><br /> <br /> <b><i>Infernal Hide: </i></b><i>The Demon\u2019s </i>hide is so touch that it can soak aggravated damage.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Hellfire: </i></b>By making a successful Dexterity + Brawl attack against an opponent, <i>The Demon </i>hurls hellfire at his opponent. The attack does +2 aggravated damage<br /> <br /> <b><i>Face of Evil: </i></b><i>The Demon\u2019s </i>mien is so unclean that mortals that gaze upon it suffer the lunacy condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Frailties: </b><i>The Demon </i>suffers aggravated damage from stepping on hollowed ground or touching holy objects. <i>The Demon </i>suffers non-soakable bashing damage from hearing prayers spoken by one of the truly faithful. <i>The Demon\u2019s </i>powers will not work on the truly faithful, the truly innocent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T20:21:39-07:00","id":1450907,"title":"","content":"Can\u2019t give out anything articulate right now, but I see the concept of \u2018soaking\u2019 damage up there \u2014 pretty sure that\u2019s a WoD concept, not CofD.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T21:17:16-07:00","id":1450908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446635-true-fae-titles?p=1450907#post1450907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can\u2019t give out anything articulate right now, but I see the concept of \u2018soaking\u2019 damage up there \u2014 pretty sure that\u2019s a WoD concept, not CofD.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I wanted to emphasize that with the exception of cold iron and it's frailties, most damage just bounces off the demon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T21:18:28-07:00","id":1450909,"title":"","content":"Another idea I am playing with is that if you wound the demon, fire comes out of the wound potentially wounding/killing the attacker.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T21:29:27-07:00","id":1450911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446635-true-fae-titles?p=1450909#post1450909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another idea I am playing with is that if you wound the demon, fire comes out of the wound potentially wounding/killing the attacker.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You know... a lot of these Titular Beings (I'm calling these that in my mind <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) look like they could be 'normal' Horrors, from the CofD core and Hunter 2E, with many of their powers being Dread Powers both existing and homebrewed. It's already canon that Fae Titles can take many forms, so maybe these Titulars really are Horrors?<br /> <br /> EDIT: Changeling 2E core also has Dread Powers, trimmed and modified for hobgoblins and Huntsmen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 06-04-2021, 12:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-04T14:01:46-07:00","id":1450982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446635-true-fae-titles?p=1450911#post1450911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> EDIT: Changeling 2E core also has Dread Powers, trimmed and modified for hobgoblins and Huntsmen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, but I wanted to give the Gentry powers unique from Huntsmen and Hobgoblins, and emphasize the Gentries godlike qualities.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-03T18:23:37-07:00","id":1458596,"title":"","content":"In the thread on Faeifying fairytale heroes and villains into Changelings, 21C Hermit suggested a Chronicle that focused on the fairytale of The Snow Queen.<br /> <br /> Here is a title a designed for playing the Snow Queen as a Gentry/True Fae, but it can also be used for Frost Giants/Jotuns or even playing the Yuki Onna as a True Fae.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Beast of Ice and Snow</i></b><br /> <br /> The Gentry is immune to outside weather cold effects, such as avalanches, blizzards, and temperatures cold enough to cause hypothermia.<br /> <br /> The Gentry leaves no trace of themselves in the snow and can turn invisible in the lightest of snowfalls.<br /> <br /> The Gentry can merge with mist, snow, and ice as a form of concealment of defense.<br /> <br /> The Gentry is immune to all supernatural effects that inspire fear or love.<br /> <br /> The Gentry gives off an aura so cold that in encases people within 8 meters/yards of the entry in ice. This does not kill the victims, however, but allows the Gentry to capture their victims at leisure.<br /> <br /> The Gentry can extend this aura up to 16 meters/yards and use it to grab things or use it as a weapon.<br /> <br /> By spending a dot of willpower and blowing a breath of wind can create gales of wind so cold that is strips people of glamour and willpower.<br /> <br /> If the Gentry is wounded, blasts of ice come out of the wound and deal +2 aggravated damage.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-09T23:42:58-07:00","id":1459511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1446635-true-fae-titles?p=1447347#post1447347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I envision it, what the fabric of destiny got tangled in was the beliefs and fears of man born from the fables and stories they told. This gave the stories a sense of awareness and even form, which is malleable based on the stories, dreams, and fears that the true fae come to feed on, AND how the stories change.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure, would have to re-read some things, but I'm under the impression that your take on True Fae is better reflected elsewhere. Some of your ideas remember spirits from the Shadow, others from the Temenos, and others work well as anything. I'm not sure if they really give the True Fae a sense of uniqueness, and maybe your concept of how the True Fae should be already exists better expressed somewhere else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}